From 2c14296a0f7fae2fbacad74c00a9cfc44d2aab49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:01:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: a change of mode that the driver refused is
 asked for again, bounded

Kodi clears its pending modeset when it assembles the commit that carries it
(CDRMAtomic::FlipPage()). When the driver refuses the test of that commit,
DrmAtomicCommit() falls back to the request before it, which goes out in the
old mode, and nothing asks for the new mode again: the display stays in the
mode before while Kodi draws for the new one, until the next change of mode.

The change is now asked for again with the next two frames of the ordinary
output, then once every 2 s, six commits in all (CModesetRetry,
DRMModesetRetry.h), until the selected mode is on the output (CCommittedMode).
Then it is given up, and the other subsystems are told that the display was
lost and is back, as SetFullScreen() tells of a change of mode. kodi.log has
one line for the first refusal, one when the mode is taken after refusals, and
one when it is given up. An output that is meant to be off is not asked for
again.

The flag of a pending modeset is cleared as before: what waits on
ModesetPending() does not wait between the retries, and a frame of native
Dolby Vision (FlipPageTransactional()) never carries a modeset that is not
pending.

The idea of keeping the change pending until the selected mode is on the
output is CroqueMr's (libreelec-x86-DV, R1.0.0 RC3). Keeping m_need_modeset
itself up until then, as there, would in Hades make every frame of native
output allow a modeset and keep what waits on a pending modeset waiting, and
with a lasting refusal every frame would commit a refused modeset: the host
test (modesetretry_test) gives 480 such commits in 20 s for that form, and 6
for this one.
